jobs.description:
Robert Half is currently looking for a Business Operations Coordinator (m/f/x).

The company is located in Brussels and this is a full-time position within an international company active in the construction materials industry.

Your responsibilities as a Business Operations Coordinator will include:

• Organising the transportation of construction materials by road and inland waterways;
• Coordinating daily logistics flows between production sites, carriers and customers;
• Monitoring deliveries and proactively anticipating operational issues;
• Receiving, processing and following up on customer orders;
• Acting as the main point of contact for customers and partners across the Benelux, Germany and France;
• Resolving customer queries and ensuring a high level of customer satisfaction;
• Supporting commercial activities, including CRM updates and prospecting follow-up;
• Managing commercial and logistics administration;
• Preparing customer invoicing and checking supplier invoices;
• Maintaining accurate customer, supplier and carrier databases;
• Preparing regular operational reports.

The required qualifications for this Business Operations Coordinator position are:

• Bachelor's degree in Logistics, Business Administration or a related field is preferred;
• Initial experience in logistics, supply chain or B2B customer service;
• Experience within the construction materials industry is considered an asset;
• Excellent command of Dutch and French, with a good knowledge of English;
• Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously;
• Proactive, solution-oriented and customer-focused mindset;
• Ability to work independently as well as part of a team;
• Good knowledge of Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, Outlook and Teams).

Are you an experienced CE Driver with a passion for cars and international transport? As an International Car Transport Driver, you will ensure the safe and timely delivery of vehicles across Germany, the Benelux, France, and Austria, while representing the company with professionalism at every customer location.

Your responsibilities?

• Transport passenger vehicles safely and efficiently across Germany, the Benelux, France, and Austria, ensuring timely pick-up and delivery;

• Load and unload vehicles in accordance with safety procedures and quality standards;

• Carry out a thorough visual inspection of every vehicle before collection and upon delivery, reporting any damage accurately;

• Follow transport instructions, customer requirements and operational procedures with great attention to detail;

• Provide customers with a professional and customer-focused service throughout every assignment;

• Represent the company as a reliable ambassador through safe driving, clear communication and a professional attitude.

What makes you the ideal candidate?

• Valid CE driving licence with Code 95;

• Experience as an international CE driver is an advantage, while experience in car transport is a strong asset;

• Excellent knowledge of traffic regulations and a safe, defensive driving style;

• Good command of English and/or German to communicate effectively with customers and colleagues;

• Solid knowledge of the European road network and the ability to organise international transport efficiently;

• Flexible, punctual and customer-oriented approach with respect for procedures and quality standards;

• Sharp eye for vehicle inspections and a strong sense of responsibility when loading, transporting and delivering vehicles.

Are you passionate about improving business processes through SAP and eager to work in an international manufacturing environment? As a SAP SD Consultant, you will play a key role in the implementation, optimisation and rollout of SAP solutions, supporting the business from analysis through to successful go-live.

Your responsibilities?

• Research new SAP functionalities and translate business needs into efficient system solutions;

• Develop new processes and optimise existing SAP SD processes within an international manufacturing environment;

• Roll out SAP templates to new factories and countries while working closely with business process owners;

• Participate in blueprint and fit-gap analyses to map business processes and functional requirements;

• Translate business requirements into functional designs, configure the system and prepare both functional and technical specifications;

• Document, test and validate new functionalities while supporting users during acceptance testing and go-live;

• Contribute to projects from initial analysis through implementation while working with the latest SAP technologies, including SAP S/4HANA.

What makes you the ideal candidate?

• Strong knowledge of SAP SD (Sales & Distribution) and related business processes;

• You can look back on a minimum of 4 years related experience;

• Understanding of manufacturing environments and production processes;

• Analytical, solution-oriented and proactive approach to problem solving;

• Ability to work independently while thriving in an informal, collaborative environment;

• Excellent command of English. Knowledge of Dutch or French is considered an asset;

• Willingness to travel occasionally within Europe;

• Ability to debug programming code is a valuable advantage.

As a Freight Forwarder, you are responsible for the end-to-end coordination and follow-up of export shipments by seafreight. Your day-to-day responsibilities include:


• Managing export files from A to Z for both FCL and LCL shipments;

• Maintaining daily contact with customers and proactively monitoring their shipments;

• Organizing and coordinating pre-carriage and on-carriage transport with logistics partners;

• Liaising with shipping lines for operational follow-up;

• Working closely with the customs team to ensure accurate and compliant documentation;

• Ensuring correct invoicing and administrative processing of shipments;

• Monitoring and adhering to all applicable quality, safety, and compliance standards.

As a Freight Forwarder, you bring the following qualifications and skills:


• Several years of experience in freight forwarding, with a strong focus on ocean freight exports;

• Fluent in English and/or Dutch;

• Comfortable working with new IT systems and logistics software;

• Able to work independently, accurately, and customer-focused;

• Strong organizational skills and the ability to efficiently manage multiple files and priorities simultaneously.

Job description
 You will work as an independent freelance dentist within a mobile dental team. The collaboration is 
flexible and can be combined with a dental practice or professional activity in your home country. 
You will mainly treat patients with substantial and often complex dental care needs. As many patients 
have postponed dental care for a long time. Solid clinical experience, including extractions, restorative 
dentistry and endodontic treatment, is therefore important. 
In addition to clinical work, we expect a cooperative attitude and willingness to assist with the practical organization of the mobile dental unit.


Practical working arrangement
 The collaboration starts with a five-day paid trial. During this first working period, you will get to know 
our way of working, our team and our patient groups. At the same time, we will evaluate whether 
there is a good professional and human fit. 
An evaluation meeting will be scheduled during or immediately after this trial period, covering: 
• Friendliness and helpfulness towards patients and team members; 
• technical and clinical skills; 
• collegiality and team spirit; 
• punctuality and reliability; 
• alignment with the mission, values ​​and strategy of The Mobile Dentists;













